Ok, I will:

1. I will define Token and TokenType in the global namespace and expose tokenize inside simple_tokenizer.
2. I will scan the input left to right, skipping whitespace and comments, and use longest-match logic for operators.
3. I will parse identifiers, numbers, and strings with dedicated helper predicates, decoding string escapes and handling invalid escapes or unterminated literals by throwing.
4. I will treat number dots and exponents carefully, only including them when followed by valid digits.
5. I will validate every character so unsupported symbols cause an exception rather than being silently ignored.

Here are the diffs for those changes:

```diff
--- simple_tokenizer.cpp
+++ simple_tokenizer.cpp
@@ ... @@
-#include <string>
