Ok, I will:

1. I will implement MinDeque using two stacks, one for the front half and one for the back half.
2. Each stack will store pairs of values and the minimum value seen so far in that stack.
3. When popping from an empty stack, I will transfer all elements from the other stack, reversing them.
4. The global minimum is the smaller of the two stack minimums, or the only stack's minimum if one is empty.
