3. From each reachable mask, I try adding each unused element and allow it only when all required predecessors are already present.
4. The answer is dp[all elements]; for nonempty n, a zero answer means the constraints contain a cycle, so I throw invalid_argument.
5. Duplicate constraints are harmless because each check simply repeats the same predecessor requirement, and the empty set returns one ordering.

