2. I extract the bits that changed, shift them right past the lowest bit and the carry, and OR them back to preserve the number of set bits.
3. I return zero when the value is zero, when no higher number with equal popcount exists, or when the carry overflows 64 bits.
4. For the previous value, I take the 64-bit complement and find the next value with the same popcount, then complement the result back.
