I return empty and degenerate matrices unchanged, then process each complete concentric layer independently. For each layer, I collect its cell coordinates in clockwise order starting from the top-left corner. I reduce the requested rotation modulo the layer perimeter and adjust negative remainders to be non-negative. Finally, I copy old values back into shifted positions, which handles counter-clockwise and clockwise rotations while leaving incomplete center rows, columns, or cells untouched.

