I normalize the input to lowercase letters only and count each letter. If more than one letter count is odd, I return no palindromes because a palindrome is impossible. I build the left half from half of each letter count and record the single middle letter when one exists. I generate each distinct permutation of that half in lexicographic order, mirror it, and insert the middle letter when needed. This yields unique palindromes in lexicographic order, and an input with no letters produces one empty palindrome.

