2. I represent the growing count as little-endian base-1e9 digits so results can exceed fixed-width integer limits.
3. Starting from D(1) = 0, I iterate i from 2 to n, multiply the digit vector by i, then add 1 when i is even or subtract 1 when i is odd using D(i) = i*D(i-1) + (-1)^i.
4. Finally, I format the base-1e9 chunks as a canonical decimal string with no leading zeros.

