2. I will use backtracking to try assigning each interval to an allowed resource that is free at its start time.
3. For each resource, I maintain the end time of the last assigned interval; a resource is available if its last end is less than or equal to the current interval's start.
4. If a complete assignment is found, I map the assignments back to the original interval order and return them.
