Ok, I will:

I compute the minimum deletions using a two-dimensional DP table where dp[start][end] stores the fewest deletions needed to make that substring a palindrome. For equal endpoint characters, I reuse the inner substring value, treating a length-two palindrome as zero. Otherwise, I try deleting the left or right character and take the smaller result plus one. Empty and one-character strings return zero immediately, and null input throws IllegalArgumentException; comparisons are case-sensitive and treat every character literally.

