2. I convert the integer part to a BigInt to preserve precision, then to the target base by repeated division.
3. For the fractional part, I represent it as a rational number using BigInt numerator and denominator, then generate up to ten digits in the target base by repeated multiplication.
4. I round the tenth digit using half-up rounding, propagate any carry into the integer part, and strip trailing zeros.
5. I handle negative zero, invalid digits, multiple decimal points, and bases outside 2–36 by throwing errors.

