Ok, I will:

1. I start with a gcd helper that works on absolute values so reduction is sign-agnostic.
2. In simplify I move a negative sign off the denominator onto the numerator, special-case a zero numerator to 0/1, and divide both parts by their gcd.
3. For rounding I split the fraction into a floor quotient and a non-negative remainder using integer arithmetic, then add one when twice the remainder reaches the denominator, so exact halves go towards positive infinity.
4. toMixedNumber reduces first and builds the string from the absolute whole part and remainder, keeping the minus sign at the front and omitting empty parts.
5. Every function rejects a zero denominator before doing any work.

